{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + avgpool + weighted) at 0.706 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l the best image encoder, and multiprofile > singleprofile. The one remaining uncertainty is aggregation: transformer underperformed avgpool with pca_n2000 (config_037: 0.586 vs config_009: 0.635), but scvi_n200 produces a richer learned representation that may benefit more from attention-based aggregation than a static PCA projection. config_019 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted) directly tests this hypothesis while keeping the proven weighted fusion. This is the only untested configuration with a realistic chance of exceeding 0.706, since all other untested scvi_n200+vit_l variants either use concat (weaker evidence) or singleprofile (weaker evidence). Expected cost is moderate (~5–7 GPU hours), comparable to config_037 (4.55) and config_032 (4.82), since scvi_n200 is a compact encoder and the transformer aggregation adds only modest overhead over avgpool."
}

